 "note": [
  "The dungeon arena on the BARE plate (1536x1024) — RaidPrep, RaidView and Results",
  "for the dungeon encounters.",
  "",
  "NO ambient actors, for the same reason as the cave: spec 09 §4.3 row 5 gives the",
  "twelve combatants to the raid screen, from the party that actually departed.",
  "",
  "This plate is braziers, so it is the one scene where the fire sprites earn their",
  "keep: fourteen of them, each on a painted bowl, each on its own phase so the room",
  "does not pulse in unison. The cyan geyser on the pentagram (~962,230) is the",
  "encounter's own light and is deliberately cold against all that orange — it is",
  "where a boss will stand.",
  "",
  "Checked with `python tools/art/preview_scene.py stage_arena_dungeon --view raidview --marks`.",
  "",
  "`marks` (W1-STAGE, STAGE-01/06): `view` (0,-280) shows plate rows 280..1015, so the upper",
  "dais with the geyser (870,200) is OFF the band — the party stands on the hall floor below",
  "the stairs and the boss on the lower ritual circle (965,885), which is where this scene's",
  "one cold light, its pulse and its motes now are; the two upper-brazier ember emitters",
  "moved to in-band braziers. Q-96 is ruled (2026-09-15): every raid encounter (E1-E5) fights",
  "here — SceneStage.arena_for.",
  "",
  "The ritual geyser pulses and its pool shimmers: this plate's one cold light is the thing",
  "a boss stands on, so it is the thing that should be moving.",
  "",
  "W7-STAGE (2026-09-15; UI-21, BL-103): the party across the hall floor below the stairs at an 84px",
  "pitch, ranks staggered by half a pitch and 44px apart (the second rank to the RIGHT — the bridge's",
  "near parapet is left of x 470 on the y 648 row); the boss at 2x on the ritual circle's right half,",
  "feet (990, 900): a 2x Main Boss spans x 835..1145 and clears the front rank's rightmost figure",
  "(722 + 39) by 74, a 400px footprint by 29; the right brazier's flame (1176..1192) stays clear, the",
  "left one (900..916, feet 796) stands BEHIND the boss and is covered — depth-correct, a creature on",
  "the circle is nearer the eye than a brazier on the far edge. `boss.floor` is the circle's stone."
 ],
